qs.append({"q":"Which of the following factors is identified in the chapter as having (perhaps unintentionally) undermined caste consciousness during British rule?","o":["Creation of private property in land and free sale of land, which upset traditional caste-vocation linkages","Deliberate abolition of the caste system by the colonial government","Complete prohibition of caste-based marriage by British law","Reservation of government jobs exclusively for lower castes"],"a":0,"e":"The introduction of private property in land, free sale of land, modern commerce/industry, urbanisation, and equality before law weakened the traditional link between caste and vocation, without any deliberate colonial intent to abolish caste."})

qs.append({"q":"Which organisation, while crusading against the disintegration of Hindu society into sub-castes, aimed at reconstructing society on the original four-fold (chaturvarna) division while upholding the right of even the lowest castes to study the scriptures?","o":["Arya Samaj","Brahmo Samaj","Prarthana Samaj","Ramakrishna Mission"],"a":0,"e":"The Arya Samaj sought to reconstruct Hindu society on the original chaturvarna basis while upholding the right of all castes, including the lowest, to study the scriptures."})

qs.append({"q":"Jyotiba Phule, who led a movement against Brahminical domination of Hindu society in Maharashtra, belonged to which social background and gave special priority to which cause?","o":["A low-caste Mali family; he prioritised education of lower castes, especially girls","A Brahmin family; he prioritised Sanskrit education","A Kshatriya family; he prioritised military reform","A Parsi family; he prioritised age of consent legislation"],"a":0,"e":"Jyotiba Phule, born in a low-caste Mali family, prioritised educating lower castes and especially girls, opening several schools for this purpose."})

qs.append({"q":"Dr B.R. Ambedkar's Mahad Satyagraha (March 1927) is significant because:","o":["He led about 2,500 'untouchables' to the Chawdar tank in Mahad and drank water from it to assert the right to public water sources","He organised the burning of the Manusmriti for the first time in Indian history","He founded the All India Scheduled Castes Federation as its outcome","It resulted immediately in a constitutional ban on untouchability"],"a":0,"e":"At Mahad, Ambedkar led a procession of about 2,500 untouchables to the Chawdar tank and drank water from it to assert their right to use public water sources previously denied to them."})

qs.append({"q":"Following the Mahad Satyagraha, in December 1927 Dr Ambedkar and his colleagues performed which symbolic act at the same location?","o":["Burnt the Manusmriti","Built a new temple open to all castes","Organised the first All India Depressed Classes Conference","Founded the Bahishkrit Hitakarini Sabha"],"a":0,"e":"In December 1927, Ambedkar and his colleagues burnt the Manusmriti at Mahad as a gesture against caste-based inequality."})

qs.append({"q":"The Bahishkrit Hitakarini Sabha, established by Dr Ambedkar in 1924 to highlight the grievances of the dalits, had which motto?","o":["Educate, Agitate and Organise","Annihilation of Caste","One religion, one caste, one God for mankind","Back to the Vedas"],"a":0,"e":"The motto of the Bahishkrit Hitakarini Sabha, founded by Ambedkar in 1924, was 'Educate, Agitate and Organise'."})

qs.append({"q":"Sri Narayana Guru, who led a lifelong struggle against upper caste domination in Kerala, coined the slogan:","o":["\"One religion, one caste, one God for mankind\"","\"Educate, Agitate, Organise\"","\"Back to the Vedas\"","\"Annihilation of Caste\""],"a":0,"e":"Sri Narayana Guru's slogan was 'One religion, one caste, one God for mankind'; his disciple Sahodaran Ayyappan later modified it to 'no religion, no caste, no God for mankind'."})

